158 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 101 0 R
/E (The database is designed to efficiently manage and organize all information related to groups, members, expenses, budgets, and settlements. PostgreSQL is used as the relational database management system, ensuring data integrity through primary keys, foreign keys, constraints, and transactions. The database structure enables accurate expense calculations, secure storage of financial records, and efficient retrieval of information. The system consists of four major tables: expense_groups, which stores group details and budgets; members, which stores member information linked to groups; expenses, which records all expense transactions; and expense_splits, which maintains expense-sharing details among members. This structured design ensures consistency, scalability, and reliable management of group financial data.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
